$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The procedure for Eq. 6. In a glove box, a vial was charged with 2a (120
mg, 0.76 mmol) and a solution of Pd(OAc)2 (0.56 mg, 2.5 μmol) and L (2.0
mg, 5.0 μmol) in toluene (1.0 mL), and the resulting solution (solution
A) was stirred for 10 min at room temperature. To another vial, (IPr)CuCl
(6.1 mg, 13 μmol), NaOMe (41 mg, 0.76 mmol), B2(pin)2 (96 mg, 0.38 mmol),
16 (90 mg, 0.25 mmol), 1e (39 mg, 0.25 mmol), toluene (1.0 mL) and the
solution A were added in this order. The resulting mixture was stirred
for 2 h at 80 ºC. After the reaction, all the volatiles were removed in
vacuo. The yield was determined by 1H NMR with 1,3,5-trimethoxybenzene as
an internal standard. 3p. 3a. 3p: Rf 0.30 (hexane:ethyl acetate = 20:1).
1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.79-7.75 (m, 3H), 7.70 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H),
7.45-7.23 (m, 7H), 7.14 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 4.46 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H),
1.71-1.68 (m, 2H), 1.042 (s, 6H), 1.037 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 101
MHz): δ 146.3, 144.0, 133.4, 132.0, 128.2, 127.8, 127.7, 127.5, 126.9,
126.0, 125.8, 125.4, 125.2, 83.1, 46.5, 24.6, 19.2 (a signal for
sp2-carbon overlap with others); HRMS-APCI(+) (m/z): [M+Na]+ calcd for
C24H27BO2Na, 381.1996; found, 381.1987. 3a: Rf 0.24 (hexane:ethyl acetate
= 95:5). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.28-7.22 (m, 8H), 7.15-7.11 (m, 2H),
4.28 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 1.60 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 1.05 (s, 12H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 101 MHz): δ 146.6, 128.2, 127.6, 125.9, 83.1, 46.5, 24.6, the
carbon directly attached to the boron atom was not detected due to
quadrupolar relaxation; HRMS-EI(+) (m/z): [M]+ calcd for C20H25BO2,
308.1948; found, 308.1941.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternative preparation shown, glovebox used,
Suzuki-Miyaura cross coupling, Miyaura Borylation reaction, inverse
addition (stage 2), 93% of
4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-2-[1-phenyl-2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)ethyl]-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
compound is recovered (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
